-- title:
--   No configuration with five or more cells
-- statement:
--   A configuration with $k$ cells consists of normalized centroids $z_j$ and masses $P_j$. They satisfy $\sum z_j=0$, $\sum|z_j|^2=1$, $\sum P_j=1$, decreasing norms, obtuseness, $|z_j|\le\frac23$, $P_j\le\frac12$, quadratic and linear mass bounds, and pair inequalities for residuals. If $k\ge5$ then
--   $$
--   \text{no configuration with }k\text{ cells exists.}
--   $$
--
--   Together with the four-cell case, this rules out every counterexample with at least four cells.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Probability/GaussianPropeller/Elimination.lean#L40-L81

